    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\nDeepSpeed's native AIO tests can hang due to a deadlock during AIO handle destruction.\r\n\r\nThe Python thread holds the GIL while waiting for the AIO worker threads to exit. A worker may need that same GIL to release its last PyTorch tensor reference, leaving both threads waiting indefinitely.\r\n\r\n#7727 and #8196 addressed related problems by releasing the GIL in `aio_handle.wait()` and blocking read/write calls. However, those fixes do not cover handle destruction, where the same GIL-related deadlock remains possible.\r\n\r\nThese are examples of CI workflow runs that seemed to get stuck because of this issue:\r\n- https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/actions/runs/38673265097/job/116221122826\r\n- https://github.com/deepspeedai/DeepSpeed/actions/runs/38683066926/job/116251793809\r\n\r\n## Approach\r\n\r\nRelease the GIL around the shared AIO/GDS base handle's worker shutdown and join sequence when destruction entered with it held. Preserve the existing path when destruction already runs without the GIL.\r\nAdd a native regression test that verifies another Python thread can make progress while an AIO handle is destroyed.\r\n\r\nThis PR will mitigate the flakiness of the CI tests.",
    "changed_files": 2,
